meta {
  name: 07 Plaid (direct)
  seq: 8
}

headers {
  PLAID-CLIENT-ID: {{plaidClientId}}
  PLAID-SECRET: {{plaidSecret}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

script:pre-request {
  // These requests call Plaid itself, not the Achalara backend, and need no
  // Achalara sign-in. They create their own throwaway sandbox login, so they never
  // touch a real one.
  //
  // With no keys they are skipped, not failed, so a run on a machine without
  // Plaid keys stays green. They never run against production: the sandbox calls
  // (/sandbox/...) do not exist there, and a production login holds real accounts.
  const base = bru.getEnvVar('plaidBaseUrl') || '';
  if (!bru.getEnvVar('plaidClientId') || !bru.getEnvVar('plaidSecret')) {
    bru.runner.skipRequest();
  } else if (!base.includes('sandbox')) {
    throw new Error('plaidBaseUrl must be https://sandbox.plaid.com: these requests create and remove test logins.');
  }
}

docs {
  Plaid's sandbox, called directly: the quickest way to see exactly what Plaid sends
  before the backend reads it (the shape `plaid_reader.py` works from).

  Set `plaidBaseUrl` (https://sandbox.plaid.com), `plaidClientId` and `plaidSecret`
  (the **sandbox** secret, `PLAID_SECRET_SANDBOX` in `backend/.env`) in your private
  environment. Run them in order: each one uses what the one before it stored
  (`plaidPublicToken`, `plaidAccessToken`).

  The sandbox login is Plaid's `user_good` at First Platypus Bank: a checking and a
  savings account, a CD, a credit card, a money market, an IRA, a 401(k), a student
  loan and a mortgage.
}
